  "manual_review": [
    "The guard reads the source of backend/app; it does not run it. It sees which modules can send a request and which hosts are written out. These it cannot see, and each stays a reviewer's responsibility:",
    "A new request inside a module that is already registered, to a host that is not written as a literal: one built from a setting, a variable or another service's answer. Review every change to a registered module for a new destination, and add the row. A new caller of a registered module is not a blind spot: it fails until it is added to reviewed_callers, and adding it is the moment to check what the call sends.",
    "Indirect callers: callers of reviewed wrapper services are not traced transitively. reviewed_callers lists the modules that call into a registered sender directly. A module that calls one of those callers, such as garden_notification_service.deliver(...) or NotificationOrchestrator().handle_notifications(...), reaches the sender through it and is not listed or checked. Review a new use of a wrapper service for what it causes to be sent.",
    "An import whose module name is computed: importlib.import_module(name) or __import__(name) with a variable, and getattr on what they return. A name written out as a string is read and held to the registry like any import, so only a computed one is a blind spot. It has to be acknowledged under dynamic_imports with its reason, and the reviewer checks what it can load.",
    "A package that arrives without being declared: installed by apt or another system package manager, or already in a base image. Packages named in backend/requirements-*.txt, in a Dockerfile's pip install or pip wheel line, and in pyproject.toml are read and have to be classified; nothing else is.",
    "Code outside backend/app: backend/scripts, backend/download_model.py, custom_components (the Home Assistant integration, which runs on the owner's Home Assistant and talks to this app), the telemetry worker, and anything vendored. None of it is scanned.",
    "A subprocess (ffmpeg, git) or OpenCV given a network address instead of a local file. Both are used on local files only; a change that passes them a URL is an outbound request the guard cannot see.",
    "What a request carries. The registry names destinations; the wording of what is sent is held by the per-locale disclosure tests, and has to be updated by hand when a payload gains a field."
  ]
}
